Package: plsnip
Title: A 'pls' Engine for 'parsnip' Partial Least Squares Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Pietro", "Franceschi", , "pietro.franceschi@fmach.it", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Registers the 'pls' package (Mevik and Wehrens, 2007,
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v018.i02>) as an engine for the partial least squares
    model 'parsnip::pls()', so that PLS regression and PLS discriminant
    analysis (PLS-DA) can be used in 'tidymodels' workflows without
    'mixOmics'. Class probabilities for PLS-DA are obtained from linear
    discriminant analysis on the PLS scores (or, optionally, a softmax of the
    predicted dummy responses). Predictions for every number of components
    are obtained from a single fit, so tuning the number of components costs
    one fit per resample.
